/**
 * Week 2 — Justice (Iustitia).
 *
 * Justice itself, not as outcome but as the constant and perpetual will
 * to render each their due. The week sits with Aquinas, Augustine,
 * Cicero, and Roman law roots, then turns the screws of the definition
 * against the working life of an advocate.
 */
